From: Marcin <91057909+mskpluk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:25:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GUI] Reload the skin when the screen aspect ratio changes

Windows kept in memory keep the skin coordinates they were loaded with.
After the screen or the window changes to another aspect ratio, they are
drawn in the old coordinate space, e.g. squashed into the top three
quarters of a 16:9 screen after starting in 4:3.

Reload the skin when the new resolution makes the skin pick another of
its resolutions, except during screen calibration. A resize during video
playback is picked up when playback stops. While Kodi is starting or an
add-on window or dialog is open, the reload waits, as it would empty what
the add-on filled in from code. The reload waits until the resizes have
settled for 500 ms, so dragging a window edge across several aspect
ratios reloads the skin once.

Fixes #25875
---
 xbmc/addons/Skin.cpp                          | 17 +++-
 xbmc/addons/Skin.h                            |  7 ++
 .../ApplicationMessageHandling.cpp            | 84 ++++++++++++++++++-
 xbmc/application/ApplicationMessageHandling.h | 10 +++
 4 files changed, 115 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/addons/Skin.cpp b/xbmc/addons/Skin.cpp
index c9c893a..418b09c 100644
--- a/xbmc/addons/Skin.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/addons/Skin.cpp
@@ -255,11 +255,24 @@ void CSkinInfo::Start()
   {
     // find the closest resolution
     const RESOLUTION_INFO& target = CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetResInfo();
-    const RESOLUTION_INFO& res = *std::ranges::min_element(m_resolutions, closestRes(target));
-    m_currentAspect = res.strId;
+    const auto res = std::ranges::min_element(m_resolutions, closestRes(target));
+    m_currentAspect = res->strId;
+    m_currentResolution = std::ranges::distance(m_resolutions.begin(), res);
   }
 }
 
+bool CSkinInfo::IsResolutionChanged() const
+{
+  if (m_resolutions.empty())
+    return false;
+
+  // compare the entry, resolutions found in the skin directory have no aspect string
+  const RESOLUTION_INFO& target = CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetResInfo();
+  return std::ranges::distance(m_resolutions.begin(),
+                               std::ranges::min_element(m_resolutions, closestRes(target))) !=
+         m_currentResolution;
+}
+
 std::string CSkinInfo::GetSkinPath(const std::string& strFile,
                                    RESOLUTION_INFO* res,
                                    std::string_view strBaseDir /* = "" */) const
